      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's solve the problem step-by-step.\n\n1. Identify the first five prime numbers.\n2. Calculate their sum.\n3. Identify the sixth prime number.\n4. Find the remainder when the sum of the first five prime numbers is divided by the sixth prime number.\n\n**Step 1: Identify the first five prime numbers.**\n\nThe first five prime numbers are:\n\\[ 2, 3, 5, 7, 11 \\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate their sum.**\n\nThe sum of the first five prime numbers is:\n\\[ 2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 \\]\n\nLet's add these numbers:\n\\[ 2 + 3 = 5 \\]\n\\[ 5 + 5 = 10 \\]\n\\[ 10 + 7 = 17 \\]\n\\[ 17 + 11 = 28 \\]\n\nSo, the sum of the first five prime numbers is:\n\\[ 28 \\]\n\n**Step 3: Identify the sixth prime number.**\n\nThe next prime number after 11 is 13. Therefore, the sixth prime number is:\n\\[ 13 \\]\n\n**Step 4: Find the remainder when the sum of the first five prime numbers is divided by the sixth prime number.**\n\nWe need to find the remainder when 28 is divided by 13. We perform the division:\n\\[ 28 \\div 13 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nThis can be written as:\n\\[ 28 = 13 \\times 2 + 2 \\]\n\nThus, the remainder is:\n\\[ 2 \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
